title: Events
act: Mine
location: Gallery
scenario: The collapse
when: once
when: here() == "Gallery"
---
The old gallery. Timbers lie across the floor like dropped matches, and the air is thick with dust.
Three ways lead on into the dark: the old shaft, the flooded gallery, and the long way round.
===

title: Events
act: Mine
location: Deep
scenario: The lights
when: once
when: here() == "Deep" and $oil > 0
---
The deep level. A seam of rock glows green along the far wall, and under it, carvings, line after line of them.
The lantern folk. Not ghosts. A border, written in stone.
===

title: Events
act: Mine
location: Deep
scenario: The collapse
quest: jory
when: once
when: here() == "Deep" and $oil <= 0 and $quest_jory == QuestState.Active
---
// The long way took the last of the oil: the cartographer reaches the deep level in the dark.
Your lamp gutters and goes out. The dark is total.
Somewhere close, a man coughs. You call, and he calls back, but in the dark the voice comes from everywhere at once.
You feel your way back along the wall to the lift, and ride it up.
<<set $quest_jory to QuestState.Failed>>
<<quest_changed jory>>
<<go DeepLift>>
===

title: OldShaft
act: Mine
location: Gallery
scenario: The collapse
quest: jory
---
<<if has_item("rope")>>
    You tie Bram's old rope to a timber and climb down the shaft, hand over hand.
    <<if $way == WayDown.None>>
        <<set $way to WayDown.Rope>>
    <<endif>>
    <<go OldShaft>>
<<else>>
    The old shaft drops straight into the dark. Without a rope, it is a grave.
<<endif>>
===

title: FloodedPassage
act: Mine
location: Gallery
scenario: The collapse
quest: jory
---
<<if has_item("remedy")>>
    You drink Nan's remedy. It burns all the way down, and then you are warm, warm enough for black water.
    <<take remedy>>
    <<go FloodedPassage>>
<<else>>
    The flooded gallery is black and still. You put a hand in the water and your fingers go numb at once.
    Not without something against the cold.
<<endif>>
===

title: FloodedOn
act: Mine
location: Flooded
scenario: The collapse
quest: jory
when: $way == WayDown.None
---
You wade on, chest-deep, holding the lamp over your head, until the floor rises under your feet.
<<set $way to WayDown.Flooded>>
<<go FloodedOn>>
===

title: LongWay
act: Mine
location: Gallery
scenario: The collapse
quest: jory
---
// The long way burns a measure of oil more: with none left after it, the cartographer arrives in the dark.
<<if $oil <= 0>>
    The long way winds off into the dark. Without oil, you would never come back.
<<else>>
    <<set $oil to $oil - 1>>
    <<if $oil > 0>>
        The long way winds down and down, through galleries nobody has walked in forty years. Your lamp burns low.
    <<else>>
        The long way winds down and down. Halfway, your lamp begins to gutter.
    <<endif>>
    <<if $way == WayDown.None>>
        <<set $way to WayDown.Long>>
    <<endif>>
    <<go LongWay>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Corvin
act: Mine
location: Gallery
scenario: The follower
quest: corvin
when: here() == "Gallery" and $corvin_in_mine
when: $corvin_fate == CorvinFate.Unmet
---
// The fifth fork: the steward, pinned under a timber in the gallery.
Corvin is on the floor of the gallery, a timber across his legs, his lamp broken beside him.
<<if $offer == Offer.Proof>>
    Corvin: You. With my letter in your pocket. Come to watch? #mood:angry
<<elseif $offer == Offer.Refused>>
    Corvin: The honest cartographer. Help me, or go away. #mood:angry
<<else>>
    Corvin: Thank the saints. Get this off me.
<<endif>>
Corvin: I came to see the carvings before you did. That's all. A steward's curiosity.
A notebook sticks out of his coat. You can see a border drawn in it, and the same border copied again, older-looking each time.
-> Lift the timber. <<if $oil > 0>>
    It takes a long time, and your lamp burns low while you work. But the timber moves.
    <<set $oil to $oil - 1>>
    <<set $corvin_fate to CorvinFate.Helped>>
    Corvin: I won't forget this. I don't say that often.
    <<set $corvin_in_mine to false>>
-> Lift the timber, and take the notebook while he is dazed. <<if $oil > 0>>
    You free him, and while he gasps on the floor, the notebook goes into your coat.
    <<set $oil to $oil - 1>>
    <<set $corvin_fate to CorvinFate.Robbed>>
    <<give notebook>>
    <<set $corvin_in_mine to false>>
    Corvin: My thanks. And my notebook? No? It must have fallen. #mood:angry
-> Leave him for the miners.
    <<set $corvin_fate to CorvinFate.Left>>
    Corvin: You can't leave me here! Cartographer! #mood:angry
    The miners will dig him out, in a day or two. After the fair.
<<set $quest_corvin to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed corvin>>
===

title: Corvin
act: Mine
location: Gallery
scenario: The follower
when: here() == "Gallery" and $corvin_in_mine
when: $corvin_fate == CorvinFate.Left
---
Corvin says nothing now. He is saving his breath for the miners.
===

title: Jory
act: Mine
location: Deep
scenario: The collapse
quest: jory
when: $quest_jory == QuestState.Active and $oil > 0
---
Jory: A light! Over here! My leg's caught in the rails.
You work his foot free. He can walk, slowly.
Jory: I followed the green light down. Thought it was the lantern folk come to take me. It's only a wall. Look at it.
<<set $jory_found to true>>
<<set $quest_jory to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed jory>>
<<walk Jory DeepLift>>
Jory: I'll wait at the lift. Don't be long. The oil won't be.
===

title: Jory
act: Mine
location: Deep
scenario: The collapse
when: $jory_found
---
=> Jory: At the lift when you're ready.
=> Jory: My mother will kill me. Then she'll feed me.
=> Jory: The carvings go on for twenty paces. I counted them, in the dark, by hand.
===

title: Carvings
act: Mine
location: Deep
scenario: The lights
quest: carvings
when: $quest_carvings == QuestState.Active
---
<<if $oil <= 0>>
    It is too dark to see the carvings, let alone copy them.
<<else>>
    You copy the carvings into the map, line by line. A mason's mark at each end: a circle with a line through it.
    <<if $quest_page == QuestState.Succeeded>>
        They match the charter's page. From the bridge stone, north under the hill, to the abbey's well. The true border.
    <<else>>
        A border, clearly. Where it runs above ground, you can only guess, but the stones by the bridge carry the same mark.
    <<endif>>
    <<survey carvings>>
    <<set $carvings_copied to true>>
    <<set $quest_carvings to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed carvings>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Carvings
act: All
location: Deep
scenario: The lights
when: $quest_carvings != QuestState.Active
---
The carvings glow faintly in the green light. They are on your map now, or lost to it.
===

title: DeepLift
act: Mine
location: Deep
scenario: The lights
when: $quest_carvings == QuestState.Active and $oil > 0
---
The carvings are not on your map yet. Go up anyway?
-> Go up.
    <<go DeepLift>>
-> Stay.
===
